Rule 8 / clean-room
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
OpenSSH (BSD/ISC) and LibreSSL (ISC/OpenSSL-style) are permissive OSS we may
legitimately read, port and adapt — Rule 8's HARD INVARIANT is about
reverse-engineered VMS formats/protocols and VSI/HPE source/binaries, which we
never touch. The VMS-facing surface the port speaks (TCPIP$DEVICE:, the QIO
function map, the BGn: sockaddr, the C-RTL/DECC$SOCKET contract) is from public
VSI OpenVMS TCP/IP Services docs + the already-landed executive facilities.
